## Summary
Root-level `required` validation in RapidJSON's SchemaValidator returns only `"#"` for both `instanceRef` and `schemaRef`, making it impossible to determine which validation constraint failed. Property-level `required` validation works correctly and shows proper JSON Pointer paths.

## Expected Behavior
Root-level `required` validation should provide meaningful error paths:
- `instanceRef`: Should indicate the location of the validation failure
- `schemaRef`: Should point to the schema constraint (e.g., `"#/required"`)

## Actual Behavior
Root-level `required` validation returns:
- `instanceRef`: `"#"` (not helpful)
- `schemaRef`: `"#"` (not helpful)

This makes error handling and user feedback impossible for root-level required field violations.

## Reproduction Code
```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include "rapidjson/document.h"
#include "rapidjson/schema.h"
#include "rapidjson/stringbuffer.h"
#include "rapidjson/writer.h"

using namespace rapidjson;

void processErrors(SchemaValidator& validator, const std::string& testName) {
    std::cout << "=== " << testName << " ===" << std::endl;

    StringBuffer sb;
    validator.GetInvalidSchemaPointer().StringifyUriFragment(sb);
    std::string schemaPtr = sb.GetString();

    sb.Clear();
    validator.GetInvalidDocumentPointer().StringifyUriFragment(sb);
    std::string instancePtr = sb.GetString();

    std::cout << "Error Type: " << validator.GetInvalidSchemaKeyword() << std::endl;
    std::cout << "  instanceRef: '" << instancePtr << "'" << std::endl;
    std::cout << "  schemaRef: '" << schemaPtr << "'" << std::endl;
}

void testValidation(const std::string& testName, const std::string& schemaStr, const std::string& dataStr) {
    Document schemaDoc;
    schemaDoc.Parse(schemaStr.c_str());
    SchemaDocument schema(schemaDoc);
    SchemaValidator validator(schema);

    Document dataDoc;
    dataDoc.Parse(dataStr.c_str());

    if (!dataDoc.Accept(validator)) {
        processErrors(validator, testName);
    }
}

int main() {
    // Root-level required validation (BUG)
    testValidation(
        "ROOT-LEVEL Required validation",
        R"({
            "type": "object",
            "required": ["name", "email"],
            "properties": {
                "name": {"type": "string"},
                "email": {"type": "string"}
            }
        })",
        R"({"name": "John"})"
    );

    // Property-level required validation (WORKS)
